# Pre-mortem light — V2i theme-picker seed
- date: 2026-09-27
- branch: fix/cli-254-v2i-theme-picker-seed
- lenses: [gary-klein, saltzer-schroeder, michael-feathers]
- risk-ledger: this file

## Risks

### R1 — Klein (blast radius)
The seed lands only inside the Docker image. Adopter machines are not
touched. Blast radius: harness CI only.
- Mitigation: no adopter path changes; only harness/docker/ paths edited.
- Cost if wrong: rebuild image; drop the COPY line; ship a revert.

### R2 — Klein (unmet prerequisite)
The seed assumes Claude reads ~/.claude/settings.json at startup and
respects `theme` as a first-run skip signal. If Claude v2.1.x does not
read that path OR ignores theme absent other fields, the picker still
fires.
- Falsification: read drive.log after PR merges CI; if theme picker
  still appears, the seed does not clear the gate.
- Cure path: extend fixture with a second field (onboardingComplete,
  or similar) after reading Claude's onboarding source of truth.

### R3 — Feathers (silent regression)
The seed could mask a future Claude change that adds a new onboarding
gate. Drive.log then shows the new gate; test at read-time reveals it.
- Mitigation: keep V2i drive.log as the source of truth for gate
  detection; do not hide log output.

### R4 — Saltzer-Schroeder (path traversal / permissions)
Seeded file lands with adopter:adopter ownership per COPY --chown.
No other user in the container can write to it. No path-traversal
surface because the fixture is a static file baked at build time.
- Mitigation: RUN chown -R covers /home/adopter/.claude after all
  COPYs land.

### R5 — Klein (image-size drift)
The seed adds a JSON file (~20 bytes) plus one mkdir + one COPY. Layer
count increases by two. Image size delta: negligible.
- Mitigation: none needed.

## Strongest concerns folded in
- R2 (Claude version drift) — falsification via drive.log; if picker
  reappears in a future Claude major, extend the fixture.
- R3 (masking future gates) — drive.log stays authoritative; do not
  silence it.

## Verdict
Ship. Risks are bounded and observable via drive.log.
